{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"gh api repos/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/contents/lib/hub/README.md --jq .content | base64 -d > hub-readme.md && rg -n 'Options|Create|restart|shared-world|metas|session-players|Rules|server|pause' hub-readme.md\"","aggregated_output":"33:| `shared-world` | one world for all players, run by the host's copy | what each player does, to the host; the world, from the host |\n68:<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"MIN-MAX\">\n74:- `hub:session-players`: the smallest and largest number of players the game\n77:- `hub:session-mode`: `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world`.\n127:| `server` | `true` only on a copy that hosts a shared world with no player of its own |\n176:| `left` | milliseconds until the round starts by itself; `null` while paused or starting |\n177:| `paused` | `true` while most players asked for more time |\n229:- A shared-world round is void when its host leaves, isn't ready, or has its\n273:- The hub can run the host's copy with no player of its own: `AIHub.server`\n296:## Rules\n301:  game server or public broker. Loading the game's own files is fine.\n305:  new tabs or navigating away. Quitting, restarting or returning to a title\n307:- **Create + Options is the hub's.** On a controller, holding the two\n308:  together opens the hub's corner bar; the game ignores Options while Create\n326:python3 -m http.server 8000\n330:The hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\n333:`&players=2&scenario=server`.\n367:| `hub:session-players` | `MIN-MAX`: the number of players the game takes in a session |\n368:| `hub:session-mode` | `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world` |\n397:| `card` | `{ left, paused, starting, ready, asking, asked }`, with the game's own card |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '55,95p' hub-readme.md && sed -n '245,320p' hub-readme.md && sed -n '1,90p' hub-session.js\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '55,95p' hub-readme.md && sed -n '245,320p' hub-readme.md && sed -n '1,90p' hub-session.js\"","aggregated_output":"2. The game connects and calls `ready()`.\n3. The round starts on the hub's clock, on every device at once.\n4. The game reports how it goes.\n5. The round ends when every player has a result, when the host of a shared\n   world finishes it, or when the hub calls time. The hub shows the results\n   over the game, then removes it.\n\n### Tags\n\nIn the game's `<head>`:\n\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"MIN-MAX\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"MODE\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"GOAL\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"CONTROLS\">\n```\n\n- `hub:session-players`: the smallest and largest number of players the game\n  takes in a session. The hub deals the game only when the number of players\n  is in that range.\n- `hub:session-mode`: `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world`.\n- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`: how to win and the game's\n  controls, shown on the hub's card.\n\nOptional:\n\n- `hub:session-minutes`: how many minutes a round of the game takes. The hub\n  shows it and uses it to decide when to call time.\n- `hub:webgpu` with `required`: the game cannot run without WebGPU. The hub\n  then deals it only when every player's browser has WebGPU.\n\n### The client\n\n[session.js](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js)\nis pasted into the game unmodified, as the first script in `<head>`, right\nafter `<meta charset>`. In a session it:\n\n- seeds `Math.random`, in parallel and ghost, before any of the game's own\n  scripts run, so it gives the same numbers on every copy;\nresults:\n\n- in `result()`: `stats` is `{ name: value }` and `awards` is\n  `[{ title, detail }]`, for this player;\n- in `finish()`: `stats` is `{ id: { name: value } }` and `awards` is\n  `[{ id, title, detail }]`, for each player.\n\nPlaces and points come only from the standings, `time` and `score`.\n\n---\n\n## Sending data between copies\n\n### Parallel\n\nThe copies send nothing to each other. `send()` is not used.\n\n### Ghost\n\nEach copy sends its own player's position and what the player is doing to\nthe other copies with `send()`. Each copy shows the other players' characters\nonly while they are in the same area of the game as its own player, and those\ncharacters do not affect its world. `Math.random` is seeded as in parallel.\n\n### Shared world\n\n- The host's copy (`AIHub.isHost`) runs the world. The other copies send the\n  host what their own player does, and show the world the host sends them.\n- The hub can run the host's copy with no player of its own: `AIHub.server`\n  is `true` and `AIHub.me` is not among `AIHub.players`. The host's copy runs\n  the world in that case too, with no local player, camera or input.\n- `Math.random` is not seeded. `AIHub.rng(label)` gives the same numbers on\n  every copy.\n\n### `send()` and `message`\n\n- `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` sends `data` to every other copy, or\n  to the one player `to`. It returns `false` when the message is dropped.\n- `AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => …)` receives it; `from` is the\n  sender's player id. A copy never receives its own messages. Messages sent\n  before another copy has loaded are queued for it.\n- `data` is JSON, at most 16 KB.\n- At most 20 messages a second leave each copy, with bursts up to 40; the\n  client drops the rest.\n- Reliable messages (the default) arrive in the order they were sent.\n  Messages sent with `reliable: false` may be lost or arrive out of order. An\n  unreliable message larger than about 1,200 bytes travels as several packets\n  and is lost whole if any of them is.\n\n---\n\n## Rules\n\nIn a session:\n\n- **Network only through the hub.** No WebSocket, WebRTC, or `fetch` to a\n  game server or public broker. Loading the game's own files is fine.\n- **No communication between players.** No chat, voice, emotes or custom\n  names. Names come from the hub.\n- **The page stays.** No `alert`, `confirm` or `prompt`; no `window.open`,\n  new tabs or navigating away. Quitting, restarting or returning to a title\n  screen does nothing; the hub starts and ends rounds.\n- **Create + Options is the hub's.** On a controller, holding the two\n  together opens the hub's corner bar; the game ignores Options while Create\n  is held.\n\nEverything on this page applies only in a session (`AIHub.active`). Outside\none, the game is not affected.\n\n---\n\n## Test it\n\nThe harness plays the hub: it loads the game 1–4 times on a simulated network\nand runs the checks the hub runs when a game joins the library. Serve it next\nto the game:\n/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\n\n  var framed = false;\n  try {\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\n  } catch (e) {\n    framed = true;\n  }\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(search);\n\n  var hub = {\n    version: VERSION,\n    protocol: 1,\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\n    me: null,\n    host: null,\n    isHost: false,\n    players: [],\n    mode: null,\n    seed: 0,\n    limitMs: 0,\n    round: 0,\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n    splash: false,\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\n    seeded: false,\n  };\n\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\n  function memoryStorage() {\n    var data = Object.create(null);\n    var api = {\n      getItem: function (k) {\n        k = String(k);\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\n      },\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\n      },\n      removeItem: function (k) {\n        delete data[String(k)];\n      },\n      clear: function () {\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\n      },\n      key: function (i) {\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\n      },\n    };\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\n    return new Proxy(api, {\n      get: function (t, k) {\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\n      },\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\n        return true;\n      },\n      has: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data || k in t;\n      },\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\n        delete data[k];\n        return true;\n      },\n      ownKeys: function () {\n        return Object.keys(data);\n      },\n      getOwnPropertyDescriptor: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data ? { value: data[k], writable: true, enumerable: true, configurable: true } : undefined;\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='shell.html';s=open(p).read().replace('<meta name=\\\"theme-color\\\"', '<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-2\\\">\\\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\">\\\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Cross the jungle and ring three bells to rescue Professor Pip\\\">\\\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Stick: move. Cross: jump. Square: tool. Circle: duck. Options: pause.\\\">\\\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"5\\\">\\\\n<meta name=\\\"theme-color\\\"');open(p,'w').write(s)\np='main.js';s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\\\"function unlock(){audio.unlock()\\\", \\\"function unlock(){if(net?.hubActive&&net.ended)return;audio.unlock()\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"\"'${button('\"'Retry this chapter','retry')}\\\",\\\"\"'${net.hubActive?'\"'':button('Retry this chapter','retry')}\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"async function doAction(action,el){audio.sfx\\\", \\\"async function doAction(action,el){if(net?.hubActive&&(net.ended||['start','couch','retry','replay','title','next-stage','auto'].includes(action)))return;audio.sfx\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"if(edge(9)){pause();\\\", \\\"if(edge(9)&&\"'!(net?.hubActive&&pressed(8))){pause();\")\ns=s.replace(\"function pollPads(now){padInputs.clear();\", \"function pollPads(now){padInputs.clear();if(net?.hubActive&&net.ended)return;\")\ns=s.replace(\"const active=['\"'playing','attract','transition'].includes(mode);\\\", \\\"const active=['playing','attract','transition'].includes(mode)&&\"'!(net.hubActive&&net.ended);\")\ns=s.replace(\"window.addEventListener('\"'keydown',e=>{if(e.target\\\", \\\"window.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{if(net?.hubActive&&net.ended)return;if(e.target\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"window.addEventListener('pointerdown',e=>{const type\\\", \\\"window.addEventListener('poin