cedural art and sound.',\n 'Coordinating physics, native animation, renderer recovery and shared-world lifecycle across three input methods and network seats.',\n 'none; the engine libraries and the AI Hub session client are unmodified. Recovery and game systems wrap their public APIs.',\n 'A documented built-in graphics-device recovery path that preserves the scene and simulation would be valuable.'\n]\nd['promptFeedback']=[\n 'The distinctive four-part source, complete vertical-slice scope, controller-first philosophy, and explicit attract-mode and dev-tool requirements.',\n 'The no-research rule alongside a required online integration reference. I used native source knowledge and read only the specified AI Hub integration files; dependency downloads were build inputs.',\n 'Giving four different arcade mechanics a coherent feel while supporting keyboard, controller, touch, synthesized audio and synchronized co-op in one self-contained file.',\n 'Explicitly separate prohibited source research from permitted integration documentation and dependency downloads, and distinguish required multiplayer transports from optional standalone choices.'\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nPY\nbiome format --write main.js > tests/format-report.txt\nnode --check main.js\npython3 -m json.tool ../exit-interview.json > tests/validated-interview.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
